# Design: consolidating bot, human, and model evidence

## Problem
Pick the V0.9 ruleset from three evidence sources that disagree:
bots price hidden information at zero, humans love it, model
players cannot search efficiently.

## Approach
Human redesign -> five default-off engine knobs. Hill-climb with
frozen gates, then a contest-health audit (share of games ending
in zero-cancellation crowns) that vetoes the climb's own winner,
then 3-game live probes per arm under a shared $1.50 cap.

## Key finding
The climb's greedy optimum (1-round window, no blind support)
crowns 48% of games unopposed - the same failure shape as the
V0.8 fee-2 candidate that only live play had caught before.
The audit veto reproduced that lesson without spending model
budget. Loser-pays-shame is the load-bearing stabilizer: it
turns the 2-round window from 16.7% draws to 1.8%.

## Gotchas
- challenge_radius >= duel_range never binds; duel legality
  already enforces adjacency. The humans' radius ask is really
  about arrival time, which the window handles.
- candidate_actions' rule summary told models that responses
  crown claims - wrong under window modes and confounding for
  live play until fixed and re-run.
- Greedy coordinate ascent misses interacting knobs; the audit
  gate is what caught it.

